- Evidence directory: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-big-features-2026-11-13/`, especially `findings.json`, source metadata, search snapshots, branch inventories and `memory-index-baseline.log`. Existing broad source audit is retained. Current heads: CLI `95eabf579d7aa6e5dbe994a6956c8e3fb44d4465`; Brain `834fbc88c950412c9e19b8b4cf6129e457094cba`; Graph `a11c08cab530ff86be89ac45fa3a66dfb84c4df5`; Git Sync `67dd3a4e083e4faae4417c1849035c7c4638112c`; ForgeMark `654e95a18db7ad690165b519eb151ecc4fc1e2f0`. Brain/Graph/Git Sync/ForgeMark remain at the earlier inspected source heads; CLI plugin source was fetched at its new head.
- Refreshed all 274 open CLI PRs through three pages, all 4 open Git Sync PRs and 7 open ForgeMark PRs, plus targeted all-state issues/PRs and relevant discussion/inline reviews. Public branches checked: CLI 517, Git Sync 27, ForgeMark 8; previous Brain 389-name inventory and relevant source/review scans reused at unchanged source head. Branch-name screening and scoped searches do not prove absence of private work or exhaustively review every prototype.

| ID | Proposed substantial feature | Evidence and necessary scope | Ownership / overlap | Gate decision |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ENH-004 | **Brain: persistent, revision-verified lexical memory index.** Reuse token/posting/corpus data across independent queries and hydrate only required records. | Fresh direct load+existing-ranker probe: a one-result query over 10,000 facts / 4,506,703 bytes has median 203.911 ms; 50,000 facts / 22,666,703 bytes has median 1,059.934 ms, including 312.062 ms canonical loading and 747.872 ms scoring. Three warm-file samples per size; synthetic corpus, unmodified production at current Brain head. Scope includes existing Unicode/CJK tokenization, corpus-scoped BM25 statistics, recency, family collapse, filters, revision validation, atomic derived-index publication and safe fallback. Distinct from ENH-001's member scheduling/cancellation. No prototype/speedup claimed. | No exact active implementation found in scoped public searches/reviews. The source explicitly names an inverted index as the future upgrade path; do not claim this as an original idea or previously unknown cost. #365 is the in-process BM25 implementation, #625 ranking semantics, #627 store loading; open #595 affects memory types and is adjacent. | **HOLD — strongest validation target.** Measured need and substantial scope; full design/ownership clearance for this known upgrade direction remains pending. Not a fourth READY claim. |
| ENH-005 | **CLI: reproducible project plugin environments.** A reviewable version/digest lock plus explicit trusted sync and project-scoped plugin selection, with multiple versions coexisting. | Current plugin manifests/pins and dispatch use one user-level install per plugin name. Necessary engineering includes transitive constraints, deterministic resolution, trusted source/receipt handling, versioned placement, Windows activation and data-schema compatibility. A binary rollback must not downgrade a migrated Brain store; reuse existing trust gates rather than allowing checked-out text to authorize downloads/exec. New workflow need is not independently validated. | Merged #1422 supplies global pins/minimum dependencies, not project environments. Merged #3074/#3117 add process mutexes and install rollback, not dependency lockfiles. Closed-unmerged #1752 is a Lua runtime. Their bodies and relevant reviews checked. No exact project-environment implementation found in scoped searches/current open inventory/branch-name checks. | **HOLD — product/design proposal.** Substantial; an intentional global-install model is not a reproduced defect. Product need, data contract and full ownership clearance required before implementation. |
| ENH-006 | **Git Sync: saved immutable plans with lease-checked application and execution receipts.** Review a concrete set of refs/OIDs, then execute exactly that set later. | Current `Client.Plan` is a dry run; `Client.Sync` independently discovers/plans again, and no apply-plan command/API exists in inspected source. Proposed artifact binds endpoint identity, scope/policy/object format and source/target OIDs without credentials; execution checks drift, validates desired objects and preserves expected-old CAS; receipts distinguish applied/already-applied/rejected refs. Do not promise cross-batch atomicity. New approval workflow demand not independently validated. | No exact saved-plan/apply proposal found in scoped all-state searches, 132 historical PR inventory and 27 branch names. #123/#135's concurrent ref safety is adjacent work to preserve, not claim as ours. Existing atomic-push request #46 is a distinct excluded feature. | **HOLD — product/design proposal.** Substantial API/contract work, but no current legitimate failure/measurement for the new workflow; not implementation-ready. |
| ENH-007 | **ForgeMark: multi-host distributed benchmark runs.** One immutable workload spread across remote workers, with joined results and honest missing-worker coverage. | README documents generator CPU saturation as a benchmark limit; #7 discussion mentions internal distributed k6 use. Current RunManager coordinates targets in one process. Scope includes worker identity/admission, credentials remaining on workers, unique ref namespaces, measurement/warm-up alignment, compatible latency aggregation, cancellation and failed-worker accounting. No representative saturation run or load test executed. | No exact distributed-worker implementation found in 27-PR inventory, 8 branch names, scoped issue/PR searches and #7 reviews. Existing #27 is shared-ref contention; #14/#6 are CI gates. Internal distributed k6 use is not evidence of a distributed ForgeMark implementation or a reservation. | **HOLD — product/design proposal.** Substantial, but actual workload/measurement need and ownership clearance remain to establish. |

### Explicit exclusions from this large-feature pass

- **Graph incremental indexing is claimed.** Open [#407](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407) contains `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-04-store-native-index-design.md` at its checked head: approved direction, per-file facts cache, pooled blob reads, store-native publication and incremental re-index milestones. This corrects any inference that only the implemented focused-read portion is owned. Do not pick the unimplemented design up as an unclaimed feature.
- **Git LFS sync already has an exact public request**, [git-sync #59](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/issues/59); excluded under the strict novelty rule. **Atomic pushes** already have [#46](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/issues/46).
- **Generic checkpoint handoff/export has existing reports/prototypes**, CLI [#1125](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1125), [#374](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/374), and open share/resume [#2654](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2654). Do not rename this an unclaimed portable-export flagship.
- **Editable Markdown memory round-trip reverses an explicit existing design.** [Brain #305](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/305) and current source make files a one-way projection. No direction agreement to reverse that contract, so not selected merely because the capability is absent.

