> **Overview**
> Adds **`OpenCodeAdapter`** so live consumers can follow OpenCode by re-exporting and feeding **one normalized message per line**, with **`FeedExport`**/`**Drop**` for compactions and reverts and **SHA-256 dedup** so unchanged snapshots emit nothing. Folding those records is intended to match **`Convert`** byte-for-byte (covered by tests).
> 
> **`NormalizeOpenCodeExport`**, **`IsOpenCodeV2Export`**, and **`OpenCodeNativeKey`** move into **`transcript`**; the CLI **`export_v2.go`** becomes thin wrappers. **`compactOpenCode`** now normalizes 2.x exports and builds lines via the same **`openCodeRecord`** path the adapter uses.
> 
> **`Convert`** fixes for OpenCode checkpoints/live parity: **pending/running** tools omit **`result`**; token-only assistant lines use **`content":null`**; **2.x exports** normalize correctly. **`OpenCodeSnapshotLines`** respects **`info.revert`** so undo/redo matches what OpenCode shows before the next prompt.
