This PR addresses multi-agent `entire review` runs getting stuck during the post-run “Finalizing output...” phase, and also hardens cancellation/finalization behavior so Ctrl+C doesn’t wedge output processing.

**Changes:**
- Stop finalize-phase wedging by avoiding expensive glamour rendering for large per-agent narrative output, and by adding a size cap to `mdrender.Render`.
- Ensure agent subprocess trees are terminated on context cancellation (so inherited stdout pipes don’t keep the run stuck), and keep the TUI animating during finalize with an elapsed timer suffix.
- Detach manifest persistence from the run cancellation context so finished workers’ findings are still written during a slow finalize.

