<details>
<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>

Adds per-call Claude Code usage to converted transcripts, enabling model-based pricing while preserving legacy token behavior for Cursor and Droid.

**Changes:**
- Emits model, fresh input tokens, and cache usage, including reported cache-write durations.
- Selects the highest-output usage snapshot and attributes interrupted calls to one owner.
- Extends the record format and updates documentation, tests, and expected output.

| File | Description |
| ---- | ----------- |
| `transcript/​testdata/​claude_expected.jsonl` | Adds expected model and cache usage fields. |
| `transcript/​records.go` | Defines optional per-call usage snapshots. |
| `transcript/​README.md` | Documents usage semantics and checkpoint slicing limits. |
| `transcript/​jsonl_records.go` | Tracks fragment usage and interrupted-call ownership. |
| `transcript/​jsonl_records_test.go` | Adjusts adapter tests for per-call usage. |
| `transcript/​fold.go` | Copies and emits authoritative usage snapshots. |
| `transcript/​constants.go` | Adds the unknown-model fallback. |
| `transcript/​compact.go` | Parses native usage and enables Claude-only emission. |
| `transcript/​compact_test.go` | Updates expected assistant model fields. |
| `transcript/​claude_usage_test.go` | Tests usage selection, ownership, and snapshot copying. |
</details>

